 "confidence": "medium",
 "notes": "Power supply frame wiring, 'VIEWED FROM REAR OF FRAME'. Two 16-contact D-shaped (keyed) connectors, P1 and P2, each two rows (1-8 opposite 9-16); part number not given, so kind 'other'. P1: AC mains cable to pins 7 and 16; all other P1 pins blank. P2: 1 +SENSE, 9 -SENSE, 2 +48V (linked to 3), 11 COM (linked to 10), 12 to a chassis-ground symbol, 6 +24V (linked to 5), 14 24V COM (linked to 13); 4, 7, 8, 15, 16 blank. SENSE recorded as a control_in port (remote sense leads from the load). Side sketch: M648 to LOAD with +48, +SENSE, -SENSE, 48 COM. NOTES 1: 'DO NOT CONNECT LOAD TO 48V WITH OUT SENSE LEADS ATTACHED.' Title block: Ward-Beck Systems Ltd., size B, 648-09-001, ISS. 1, DATE MAY 9/68 (file name says 1970). No signal pins and no insert."
